#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""Stand-in for the `claude` CLI. Run under the name `codex` (the `codex` file
beside it is a link to this one) it stands in for the `codex` CLI instead.

It looks and reports like the real CLI towards the app and towards a person
looking at the terminal, and never calls a model or the network. It writes no
file, except one when <dir>/keylog exists (see "Key log"). Observed behaviour of the real CLIs: docs/clawddy-refactor/cli-facts.md,
and the probes of 2026-11-23 against Claude Code 2.1.331 and Codex 0.169.0
(screens, reports, hook payloads, queueing and interrupts as described below).

What it does
- Arguments the app passes. claude: --session-id ID, --resume [ID],
  --fork-session, --name NAME, --settings FILE, --dangerously-skip-permissions,
  --model, --effort, and a positional first prompt. codex: `resume ID`,
  `fork ID`, -c/--config key=value (notify=[...] and model_reasoning_effort are
  read), --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox, --model, a positional
  first prompt. Unknown flags are accepted and ignored. `--version`,
  `claude auth status` and `codex login status` answer as the real CLIs do.
  `claude agents --json` lists the running stand-in claude sessions, found by
  their --resume or --session-id argument in the process list, as the real
  one lists its running interactive sessions.
- Terminal: raw mode, bracketed paste, a transcript above a bottom area with
  the spinner, queued prompts, the input line and the footer. claude's input
  line sits between two full-width rules: "❯" and a no-break space, then the
  text; empty it shows nothing, or `Try "edit <filepath> to…"` before the
  first prompt, or "Press up to edit queued messages" while a prompt is
  queued. codex's composer is "› " and the text, or "Ask Codex to do
  anything". Resize clears the screen and draws everything again.
- Status reports (OSC 7501): claude asks `7501;?` at start and reports only
  once the terminal answers (BEL-terminated, app=claude-code); codex reports
  always (ESC-backslash-terminated, app=codex). The first report is the sign
  the CLI reads keys: claude `idle` (or `working` with a first prompt, or
  `blocked kind=permission` on the folder-trust dialog); codex `idle` after
  its start-up `working`, none while its update dialog shows.
- claude runs the hook commands and the statusLine command of the --settings
  file with the real payload JSON on stdin: SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit,
  PreToolUse/PostToolUse (tool lines), PermissionRequest (a question), Stop,
  StopFailure, PreCompact/PostCompact (/compact), Notification (idle_prompt,
  60 s after a turn ends), SessionEnd. codex runs the notify program at the
  end of each completed turn with the JSON as its last argument, and once more
  for the title it makes after the first prompt (another thread-id).
- Keys: typing edits the line; paste inserts (newlines stay in one message);
  Return submits. While working a submitted prompt is queued: claude fires
  UserPromptSubmit for it at once, with the running turn's prompt_id; both
  CLIs fold it into the running turn at its next tool line (or its end), so
  the turn ends once, answering the latest prompt. Escape (or Ctrl-C) while
  working interrupts: claude puts the prompt back in the line only when the
  turn has shown nothing yet (and drops it from the transcript), codex never;
  codex with queued prompts submits them at once instead. With text in an idle
  line: claude clears it on Escape twice (within 0.8 s) or on Ctrl-C, which
  also arms "Press Ctrl-C again to exit"; codex clears it on Ctrl-C and
  ignores Escape. Ctrl-C twice or Ctrl-D on an empty line exits; /exit (codex
  also /quit), /login, /clear and /compact (claude) work. SIGTERM and SIGHUP
  end the session (SessionEnd reason "other") and restore the terminal.

Key log
When <dir>/keylog exists, where <dir>/bin holds this program, every key and
paste the stand-in reads is appended to <dir>/keylog/<session-id>.log, one per
line, as it decodes them: a key's name (enter, esc, ctrl-c, up, left, ...),
"char <c>" for a typed character, "paste <json string>" for a paste. The
harness's key-routing soak reads it to see which terminal each key reached.

The script file
Optional: <dir>/standin/<session-id>.json, where <dir>/bin holds this program.
claude looks under its --session-id, then its --resume id; codex under its
`resume`/`fork` id. If none exists, <dir>/standin/default.json is used if
present. Format (every key optional):

  {
    "title":   "Tide chart blank",    terminal title once a prompt is seen
                                      (default: the first words of the prompt)
    "folder":  "~/projects/tidepool", folder shown in the header (default: cwd)
    "context": 83,                    "% context left" in the footer
    "plus": 38, "minus": 9,           lines added/removed so far (status line)
    "screen":  [LINE, ...],           on screen at start, as if resumed
    "escapeAsks": {"ask": "Stop?", "options": ["Yes", "No"]}
                                      the first Escape in a turn shows this
                                      question instead of interrupting
    "trust":   true,                  claude: the folder-trust dialog first
                                      ("No, exit" selected, as the real one)
    "update":  true,                  codex: the update dialog first (Escape
                                      skips; Return on "Update now" exits)
    "steps":   [STEP, ...]            run in order, then the default behaviour
  }

  LINE is the text as it appears on screen; its first characters say what it is:
    "> text"         the person's prompt
    "⏺ Name(args)"   a tool call (a capitalised name right before "(")
    "⏺ text"         the agent's text
    "⎿ text"         a tool's result, under the call before it
    "! text"         an error
    anything else    plain text ("" is a blank line)

  STEP is one of:
    {"print": [LINE, ...], "rate": 5}      print at RATE lines a second (default 5);
                                           tool lines run PreToolUse/PostToolUse
    {"working": "Running the tests", "elapsed": 130}
                                           report working (opens a turn if none is
                                           open); spinner text; seconds already spent
    {"finish": "message", "summary": "...", "plus": 3, "minus": 1}
                                           final message: Stop hook / notify, `done`;
                                           summary is the later `done` msg (claude)
    {"ask": "Question?", "options": ["A", "B"], "header": "Layout"}
                                           blocked on a question until answered (digit,
                                           arrows + Return, or typed text + Return)
    {"fail": "login" | "usage" | "error", "text": "...", "resets": "3pm"}
                                           the turn fails: login is `blocked kind=auth`
                                           (claude), usage and error are `error`
    {"wait": 2.5}                          wait this long (ends early if a prompt
                                           starts a turn)
    {"wait": "prompt"}                     wait for a prompt; it opens the turn the
                                           next steps belong to

  A prompt submitted while no turn is open always opens a turn at once. Its
  work is the next steps, or, when no steps are left, the default turn: about
  4 seconds of tool lines, then a short message that mentions the prompt. If
  the steps run out while a turn is open, that turn ends with the default
  message. An interrupt skips the rest of the turn's steps up to and including
  its "finish" or "fail".
"""
import base64
import collections
import errno
import json
import os
import random
import re
import select
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import termios
import time
import tty
import unicodedata
import uuid

PROG = os.path.basename(sys.argv[0])
CODEX = PROG == "codex"
HARNESS = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(sys.argv[0])))
VERSION = "0.169.0" if CODEX else "2.1.331"
APP = "codex" if CODEX else "claude-code"
ST = "\x1b\\" if CODEX else "\x07"  # what ends an OSC 7501 report

def rgb(r, g, b):
    return f"\x1b[38;2;{r};{g};{b}m"

RESET, BOLD, INV = "\x1b[0m", "\x1b[1m", "\x1b[7m"
ORANGE, GREEN, GREY = rgb(215, 119, 87), rgb(78, 186, 101), rgb(153, 153, 153)
RED, BLUE, WHITE, PINK = rgb(255, 107, 128), rgb(177, 185, 249), rgb(255, 255, 255), rgb(253, 93, 177)
NBSP = "\u00a0"  # claude puts a no-break space after its "❯"
TITLE_PROMPT = ("Generate a concise, single-line task title of at most 36 characters and under five words where "
                "possible. Start with an imperative verb. Do not answer the request.\n\nUser prompt:\n")
SHADE = "\x1b[48;2;44;47;54m"
SPIN = "·✢✳✶✻✽✻✶✳✢"
BRAILLE = "⠋⠙⠹⠸⠼⠴⠦⠧⠇⠏"


# ---- arguments -------------------------------------------------------------

CLAUDE_VALUES = {"--session-id": "session", "--name": "name", "-n": "name", "--settings": "settings",
                 "--model": "model", "--effort": "effort", "--permission-mode": None, "--debug-file": None,
                 "--allowedTools": None, "--disallowedTools": None, "--add-dir": None, "--mcp-config": None,
                 "--append-system-prompt": None, "--system-prompt": None, "--fallback-model": None,
                 "--output-format": None, "--input-format": None, "--setting-sources": None}
CODEX_VALUES = {"-c": "config", "--config": "config", "-m": "model", "--model": "model", "-s": None,
                "--sandbox": None, "-a": None, "--ask-for-approval": None, "-C": None, "--cd": None,
                "-p": None, "--profile": None, "-i": None, "--image": None, "--enable": None,
                "--disable": None, "--add-dir": None}


def toml_strings(value):
    """The strings of a TOML array of strings, such as notify=["a", 'b']."""
    out = []
    for m in re.finditer(r'"((?:[^"\\]|\\.)*)"|\'([^\']*)\'', value):
        out.append(json.loads('"' + m.group(1) + '"') if m.group(1) is not None else m.group(2))
    return out


def parse_args(argv):
    o = {"session": None, "resume": None, "fork": False, "name": None, "settings": None, "model": None,
         "effort": None, "skip": False, "notify": None, "words": []}
    values = CODEX_VALUES if CODEX else CLAUDE_VALUES
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        i += 1
        if a == "--":
            o["words"] += argv[i:]
            break
        if not a.startswith("-") or a == "-":
            o["words"].append(a)
            continue
        flag, eq, v = a.partition("=")
        if flag in ("--resume", "-r") and not CODEX:
            if eq:
                o["resume"] = v
            elif i < len(argv) and not argv[i].startswith("-"):
                o["resume"] = argv[i]
                i += 1
            else:
                o["resume"] = ""  # Claude's own list of conversations
            continue
        if flag in values:
            if not eq:
                if i >= len(argv):
                    sys.exit(f"{PROG}: {flag} needs a value")
                v = argv[i]
                i += 1
            key = values[flag]
            if key == "config":
                k, _, val = v.partition("=")
                if k.strip() == "notify":
                    o["notify"] = toml_strings(val)
                elif k.strip() == "model_reasoning_effort":
                    o["effort"] = val.strip().strip("\"'")
            elif key:
                o[key] = v
            continue
        if flag in ("--dangerously-skip-permissions", "--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox", "--yolo"):
            o["skip"] = True
        elif flag == "--fork-session":
            o["fork"] = True
        # Any other flag is accepted and ignored.
    return o


def safe_name(s):
    return bool(s) and re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9._-]+", s) is not None


def load_script(keys):
    for k in [k for k in keys if safe_name(k)] + ["default"]:
        path = os.path.join(HARNESS, "standin", k + ".json")
        if os.path.exists(path):
            with open(path) as f:
                return json.load(f)
    return {}


# ---- text ------------------------------------------------------------------

def cells(s):
    n = 0
    for ch in s:
        if unicodedata.combining(ch):
            continue
        n += 2 if unicodedata.east_asian_width(ch) in "WF" else 1
    return n


def fit(segs, cols):
    """One screen row from (text, style) pieces, cut to `cols` cells."""
    out, used = [], 0
    for text, style in segs:
        keep = ""
        for ch in text:
            w = cells(ch)
            if used + w > cols:
                break
            keep += ch
            used += w
        if keep:
            out.append(style + keep + (RESET if style else ""))
        if used >= cols:
            break
    return "".join(out), used


def pad(segs, cols, style=""):
    row, used = fit(segs, cols)
    return row + style + " " * (cols - used) + (RESET if style else "")


def elapsed(s):
    s = int(s)
    if s < 60:
        return f"{s}s"
    if s < 3600:
        return f"{s // 60}m {s % 60}s"
    return f"{s // 3600}h {s % 3600 // 60}m"


def b64(text):
    return base64.b64encode(text.encode()[:2048].decode("utf-8", "ignore").encode()).decode()


def entry_of(line):
    """A script LINE as (kind, text)."""
    if line.startswith("> "):
        return ("you", line[2:])
    if line.startswith("⏺ "):
        body = line[2:]
        return ("tool", body) if re.match(r"[A-Z][A-Za-z]*\(", body) else ("text", body)
    if line.lstrip().startswith("⎿"):
        return ("out", line.lstrip()[1:].strip())
    if line.startswith("! "):
        return ("err", line[2:])
    return ("plain", line)


def tool_input(name, args):
    if name == "Bash":
        return {"command": args, "description": ""}
    if name in ("Read", "Edit", "Update", "Write"):
        return {"file_path": args}
    if name in ("Grep", "Search", "Glob"):
        return {"pattern": args}
    return {"input": args}


# ---- the program -----------------------------------------------------------

class StandIn:
    def __init__(self, o):
        self.o = o
        self.cwd = os.getcwd()
        self.first_prompt = " ".join(o["words"]) or None
        if CODEX:
            verb = o["words"][0] if o["words"] else ""
            known = o["words"][1] if verb in ("resume", "fork") and len(o["words"]) > 1 else None
            self.first_prompt = " ".join(o["words"][2 if known else 0:]) or None
            self.sid = known if verb == "resume" and known else str(uuid.uuid4())
            self.source = verb if known else "startup"
            self.script = load_script([known])
        else:
            resumed = o["resume"] or None
            self.sid = o["session"] or (resumed if not o["fork"] else None) or str(uuid.uuid4())
            self.source = "fork" if o["fork"] else "resume" if resumed else "startup"
            self.script = load_script([o["session"], resumed])
        self.resumed = self.source != "startup"
        if o["settings"]:
            s = o["settings"]
            if s.lstrip().startswith("{"):
                self.settings = json.loads(s)
            else:
                with open(s) as f:
                    self.settings = json.load(f)
        else:
            self.settings = {}
        sc = self.script
        self.context = sc.get("context", 83)
        self.plus, self.minus = sc.get("plus", 0), sc.get("minus", 0)
        self.folder = sc.get("folder") or self.cwd.replace(os.path.expanduser("~"), "~", 1)
        self.script_title = sc.get("title")
        self.escape_asks = sc.get("escapeAsks")
        self.title_base = None if CODEX else o["name"] or "Claude Code"
        self.title_shown = None
        self.status_ok = CODEX
        self.reported = None
        self.status_text = ""
        # transcript and screen
        self.entries = [("header", "")]
        for line in sc.get("screen", []):
            self.add(entry_of(line))
        self.printed = 0
        self.dyn_rows = 0
        self.dirty = True
        self.full = True
        # input
        self.inbuf = b""
        self.esc_at = None
        self.pasting = False
        self.paste = b""
        self.input, self.cur = "", 0
        self.ctrl_c_at = None
        self.esc_at_idle = None  # claude: a first Escape with text in the line
        self.dialog = None  # "trust" (claude) or "update" (codex), with the selection
        self.trusted = False  # claude runs no hook before the folder is trusted
        # turns
        self.turn_open = False
        self.turn_seq = 0
        self.turn_prompt = None
        self.turn_started = 0.0
        self.turn_prompts = []  # every prompt of the open turn, queued ones folded in
        self.turn_shown = False  # the open turn has shown something since its prompt
        self.prompt_id = None
        self.step = ""
        self.queue = []
        self.asking = None
        self.last_answer = None
        self.last_tool = None
        self.last_summary = None
        self.unclaimed = None
        self.prompts_seen = 0
        # script
        self.steps = collections.deque(sc.get("steps", []))
        self.gen = None
        self.begun = False
        self.waiting = None
        self.timers = []
        self.signal = None
        self.winch = False
        self.hung = False

    # ---- output ----
    def write(self, s):
        data = s.encode()
        while data:
            if self.hung:
                # The terminal may be gone after a hang-up; there is nothing left to restore.
                try:
                    n = os.write(1, data)
                except OSError:
                    return
            else:
                n = os.write(1, data)
            data = data[n:]

    def report(self, state, kind=None, msg=None):
        self.reported = (state, kind, msg)
        if not self.status_ok:
            self.refresh_title()
            return
        body = f"7501;state={state}" + ("" if state == "clear" else f":app={APP}")
        if kind:
            body += f":kind={kind}"
        if msg:
            body += ":msg=" + b64(msg)
        out = "\x1b]" + body + ST
        if not CODEX and os.environ.get("TERM_PROGRAM") == "ghostty":
            out += "\x1b]9;4;3;\x07" if state in ("working", "blocked") else "\x1b]9;4;0;\x07"
        self.write(out)

    def title(self, text):
        if text != self.title_shown:
            self.title_shown = text
            self.write(f"\x1b]0;{text}\x07")

    def refresh_title(self):
        if CODEX:
            base = os.path.basename(self.cwd) if not self.title_base else f"{self.title_base} | {os.path.basename(self.cwd)}"
            frame = BRAILLE[int(time.monotonic() * 10) % len(BRAILLE)] + " " if self.turn_open else ""
            self.title(frame + base)
            return
        if self.title_base is None:
            return
        glyph = "" if self.status_ok else ("◐ " if self.turn_open else "✳ ")
        self.title(glyph + self.title_base)

    # ---- hooks ----
    def run_command(self, command, stdin, timeout, label):
        env = dict(os.environ, CLAUDECODE="1", CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR=self.cwd)
        try:
            r = subprocess.run(["/bin/sh", "-c", command], input=stdin, text=True, capture_output=True,
                               timeout=timeout, cwd=self.cwd, env=env)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            self.add(("err", f"{label} timed out after {timeout}s"))
            return None
        if r.returncode != 0:
            self.add(("err", f"{label} failed with status {r.returncode}: {r.stderr.strip()[:200]}"))
        return r.stdout

    def payload(self, event, fields):
        return {"session_id": self.sid,
                "transcript_path": os.path.join(HARNESS, "standin", "transcripts", self.sid + ".jsonl"),
                "cwd": self.cwd,
                "scratchpad_dir": os.path.join(HARNESS, "standin", "scratchpad", self.sid),
                "hook_event_name": event, **fields}

    def hook(self, event, tool=None, **fields):
        if CODEX or not self.trusted:
            return
        data = json.dumps(self.payload(event, fields))
        for group in self.settings.get("hooks", {}).get(event, []):
            matcher = group.get("matcher", "")
            if matcher not in ("", "*") and tool is not None and not re.fullmatch(matcher, tool):
                continue
            for h in group.get("hooks", []):
                if h.get("type") != "command":
                    continue
                out = self.run_command(h["command"], data, h.get("timeout", 60), f"{event} hook")
                if out and out.strip().startswith("{"):
                    title = json.loads(out).get("hookSpecificOutput", {}).get("sessionTitle")
                    if title:
                        self.title_base = title
                        self.refresh_title()

    def statusline(self):
        sl = self.settings.get("statusLine")
        if CODEX or not sl or sl.get("type") != "command":
            return
        p = {"session_id": self.sid, "session_name": self.title_base or "",
             "transcript_path": self.payload("", {})["transcript_path"], "cwd": self.cwd,
             "model": {"id": self.o["model"] or "standin", "display_name": self.o["model"] or "Stand-in"},
             "workspace": {"current_dir": self.cwd, "project_dir": self.cwd, "added_dirs": []},
             "version": VERSION, "output_style": {"name": "default"},
             "cost": {"total_cost_usd": 0, "total_duration_ms": 0, "total_api_duration_ms": 0,
                      "total_lines_added": self.plus, "total_lines_removed": self.minus},
             "context_window": {"used_percentage": 100 - self.context, "remaining_percentage": self.context},
             "exceeds_200k_tokens": False}
        out = self.run_command(sl["command"], json.dumps(p), 10, "Status line")
        text = re.sub(r"\x1b\[[0-9;]*m", "", out or "").strip().splitlines()
        self.status_text = text[0] if text else ""
        self.dirty = True

    def notify(self, message):
        argv = self.o["notify"]
        if not argv:
            return
        self.run_notify({"type": "agent-turn-complete", "thread-id": self.sid, "turn-id": self.prompt_id,
                         "cwd": self.cwd, "client": "codex-tui", "input-messages": list(self.turn_prompts),
                         "last-assistant-message": message})

    def notify_title(self, prompt, title):
        """codex titles the conversation in a turn of its own, on another thread, which notifies too."""
        if self.o["notify"]:
            self.run_notify({"type": "agent-turn-complete", "thread-id": str(uuid.uuid4()), "turn-id": str(uuid.uuid4()),
                             "cwd": self.cwd, "client": "codex-tui", "input-messages": [TITLE_PROMPT + prompt],
                             "last-assistant-message": json.dumps({"title": title})})

    def run_notify(self, payload):
        r = subprocess.run(self.o["notify"] + [json.dumps(payload)], stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True,
                           timeout=10, cwd=self.cwd)
        if r.returncode != 0:
            self.add(("err", f"notify failed with status {r.returncode}"))

    # ---- transcript ----
    def add(self, entry):
        """Appends to the transcript, with one blank line before each message, as the CLIs space them."""
        blank = ("plain", "")
        if entry == blank and self.entries[-1] == blank:
            return
        if entry[0] in ("you", "tool", "text", "rule") and self.entries[-1] != blank:
            self.entries.append(blank)
        self.entries.append(entry)
        self.dirty = True

    def add_line(self, line):
        e = entry_of(line)
        self.add(e)
        if not self.turn_open:
            return
        self.turn_shown = True
        if e[0] == "tool":
            m = re.match(r"([A-Za-z]+)\((.*)\)$", e[1])
            name, args = (m.group(1), m.group(2)) if m else (e[1], "")
            self.last_tool = (name, args, "toolu_" + uuid.uuid4().hex[:24], time.monotonic())
            self.report("working", msg=f"{name} {args}"[:120])
            self.hook("PreToolUse", tool=name, tool_name=name, tool_input=tool_input(name, args),
                      tool_use_id=self.last_tool[2], prompt_id=self.prompt_id, effort=self.effort(),
                      permission_mode=self.mode())
        elif e[0] == "out" and self.last_tool:
            name, args, tid, t0 = self.last_tool
            self.last_tool = None
            self.hook("PostToolUse", tool=name, tool_name=name, tool_input=tool_input(name, args),
                      tool_response={"stdout": e[1], "stderr": "", "interrupted": False}, tool_use_id=tid,
                      duration_ms=int((time.monotonic() - t0) * 1000), prompt_id=self.prompt_id,
                      effort=self.effort(), permission_mode=self.mode())
        if e[0] == "out":
            # A prompt queued meanwhile joins the turn after the tool's result.
            self.fold_queue()

    def mode(self):
        return "bypassPermissions" if self.o["skip"] else "default"

    def effort(self):
        return {"level": self.o["effort"] or "medium"}

    # ---- turns ----
    def start_turn(self, prompt):
        self.turn_seq += 1
        self.turn_open = True
        self.turn_prompt = prompt
        self.turn_prompts = [prompt] if prompt else []
        self.turn_shown = False
        self.prompt_id = str(uuid.uuid4())
        self.turn_started = time.monotonic()
        self.step = random.choice(["Thinking", "Pondering", "Working", "Considering"])
        self.dirty = True
        if prompt is None:
            self.report("working")
            return
        self.add(("you", prompt))
        self.report("working")
        self.hook("UserPromptSubmit", prompt=prompt, prompt_id=self.prompt_id, permission_mode=self.mode())
        self.prompts_seen += 1
        if self.prompts_seen == 1 and (CODEX or not self.o["name"]):
            # About a second after the first prompt the CLI titles the conversation.
            words = " ".join(prompt.split()[:4])
            name = self.script_title or (words[:1].upper() + words[1:])

            def titled():
                self.title_base = name
                self.refresh_title()
                if CODEX:
                    self.notify_title(prompt, name)
            self.later(1.0, titled)
        self.unclaimed = prompt
        if self.waiting and self.waiting[0] in ("wait", "prompt"):
            self.unclaimed = None
            self.run_director(prompt)

    def end_turn(self):
        self.turn_open = False
        self.asking = None
        self.last_tool = None
        self.context = max(5, self.context - 2)
        self.dirty = True
        self.refresh_title()
        if not CODEX:
            seq = self.turn_seq
            self.later(60, lambda: seq == self.turn_seq and not self.turn_open and self.hook(
                "Notification", message="Claude is waiting for your input", notification_type="idle_prompt",
                prompt_id=self.prompt_id))

    def fold_queue(self):
        """Queued prompts join the running turn, which now answers the latest of them."""
        for q in self.queue:
            self.add(("you", q))
            self.turn_prompts.append(q)
            self.turn_prompt = q
        self.queue = []

    def finish(self, message, summary=None, plus=0, minus=0):
        if not self.turn_open:
            self.start_turn(None)
        self.plus += plus
        self.minus += minus
        took = time.monotonic() - self.turn_started
        self.fold_queue()
        if CODEX:
            self.add(("rule", f"Worked for {elapsed(took)}"))
            self.add(("text", message))
            self.draw()
            self.report("done")
            self.notify(message)
            self.end_turn()
            return
        self.add(("text", message))
        self.add(("plain", f"{ORANGE}✻{RESET} {GREY}Worked for {elapsed(took)}{RESET}"))
        self.draw()
        self.hook("Stop", prompt_id=self.prompt_id, effort=self.effort(), permission_mode=self.mode(),
                  last_assistant_message=message, stop_hook_active=False, background_tasks=[], session_crons=[])
        self.report("done")
        self.statusline()
        seq = self.turn_seq
        summary = summary or message.split(". ")[0].rstrip(".")[:80]
        self.last_summary = summary
        self.later(1.7, lambda: seq == self.turn_seq and not self.turn_open and self.report("done", msg=summary))
        self.end_turn()

    def fail(self, kind, text=None, resets=None):
        if not self.turn_open:
            self.start_turn(None)
        if text is None:
            if kind == "login":
                text = ("Your access token could not be refreshed because you have since logged out or signed in to another account. Run codex login."
                        if CODEX else "API Error: 401 · OAuth token has expired. Please run /login")
            elif kind == "usage":
                text = ((f"You've hit your usage limit. Try again at {resets}." if resets else "You've hit your usage limit.")
                        if CODEX else (f"Claude usage limit reached. Your limit will reset at {resets}." if resets
                                       else "Claude usage limit reached."))
            else:
                text = "API Error: Connection refused — a firewall or proxy may be blocking it (ECONNREFUSED)"
        self.fold_queue()
        self.add(("err", text))
        self.draw()
        if CODEX:
            self.report("error")
        else:
            if kind == "login":
                self.report("blocked", kind="auth", msg=text)
            else:
                self.report("error", msg=text)
            self.hook("StopFailure", error={"login": "authentication_failed", "usage": "rate_limit"}.get(kind, "server_error"),
                      last_assistant_message=text, prompt_id=self.prompt_id, effort=self.effort())
        self.end_turn()

    def ask(self, question, options, header):
        if not self.turn_open:
            self.start_turn(None)
        tid = "toolu_" + uuid.uuid4().hex[:24]
        questions = [{"question": question, "header": header or "Question", "multiSelect": False,
                      "options": [{"label": o, "description": ""} for o in options]}]
        self.asking = {"q": question, "options": options, "header": header or "Question", "sel": 0, "id": tid,
                       "questions": questions, "at": time.monotonic()}
        self.draw()
        self.hook("PreToolUse", tool="AskUserQuestion", tool_name="AskUserQuestion", tool_input={"questions": questions},
                  tool_use_id=tid, prompt_id=self.prompt_id, effort=self.effort(), permission_mode=self.mode())
        self.hook("PermissionRequest", tool="AskUserQuestion", tool_name="AskUserQuestion",
                  tool_input={"questions": questions}, permission_suggestions=[], prompt_id=self.prompt_id,
                  effort=self.effort(), permission_mode=self.mode())
        self.report("blocked", kind="question", msg=f"answer: {question} ({' · '.join(options)})")

    def answer(self, text):
        q = self.asking
        self.asking = None
        self.input, self.cur = "", 0
        answers = {q["q"]: text}
        self.hook("PostToolUse", tool="AskUserQuestion", tool_name="AskUserQuestion",
                  tool_input={"questions": q["questions"], "answers": answers, "annotations": {}},
                  tool_response={"questions": q["questions"], "answers": answers}, tool_use_id=q["id"],
                  duration_ms=int((time.monotonic() - q["at"]) * 1000), prompt_id=self.prompt_id,
                  effort=self.effort(), permission_mode=self.mode())
        if CODEX:
            self.add(("text", f"You chose: {text}"))
        else:
            self.add(("text", "User answered Claude's questions:"))
            self.add(("out", f"· {q['q']} → {text}"))
        self.last_answer = text
        self.report("working")
        if self.waiting and self.waiting[0] == "answer":
            self.run_director(text)

    def interrupt(self):
        if not (self.turn_open or self.asking):
            return
        queued, self.queue = self.queue, []
        if CODEX:
            self.add(("err", "Conversation interrupted - use /feedback if something went wrong"))
        else:
            # Only a turn that has shown nothing gives its prompt back, and drops it from the transcript.
            back = ([self.turn_prompt] if self.turn_prompt and not self.turn_shown else []) + queued
            if back and self.turn_prompt and not self.turn_shown and ("you", self.turn_prompt) in self.entries:
                i = len(self.entries) - 1 - self.entries[::-1].index(("you", self.turn_prompt))
                del self.entries[i:]
                self.full = True
            if back:
                self.input = "\n".join(back + ([self.input] if self.input else []))
                self.cur = len(self.input)
            else:
                self.add(("out", "Interrupted · What should Claude do instead?"))
        self.turn_open = False
        self.asking = None
        self.last_tool = None
        self.report("idle")
        self.refresh_title()
        if self.gen:
            self.gen.close()
        while self.steps:
            st = self.steps.popleft()
            if "finish" in st or "fail" in st:
                break
        self.unclaimed = None
        self.gen = self.director()
        self.run_director()
        if CODEX and queued:
            # "press esc to interrupt and send immediately"
            self.submit("\n".join(queued))

    # ---- the script ----
    def director(self):
        while self.steps:
            yield from self.do_step(self.steps.popleft())
        while True:
            if not self.turn_open:
                yield ("prompt",)
            self.unclaimed = None
            yield from self.default_work(self.turn_prompt or self.last_answer)

    def do_step(self, st):
        if "print" in st:
            rate = st.get("rate", 5)
            for line in st["print"]:
                self.add_line(line)
                yield ("sleep", 1.0 / rate)
        elif "working" in st:
            if not self.turn_open:
                self.start_turn(None)
            self.step = st["working"] or self.step
            self.turn_started = time.monotonic() - st.get("elapsed", 0)
            self.dirty = True
            # Claude's report names the step under way (cli-facts.md).
            self.report("working", msg=None if CODEX else self.step)
        elif "finish" in st:
            self.finish(st["finish"], st.get("summary"), st.get("plus", 0), st.get("minus", 0))
        elif "ask" in st:
            self.ask(st["ask"], st.get("options", []), st.get("header"))
            yield ("answer",)
        elif "fail" in st:
            self.fail(st["fail"], st.get("text"), st.get("resets"))
        elif "wait" in st:
            yield ("prompt",) if st["wait"] == "prompt" else ("wait", float(st["wait"]))
        else:
            raise ValueError(f"unknown step in the stand-in script: {st}")

    def default_work(self, prompt):
        words = re.findall(r"[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{2,}", prompt or "")
        w = max(words, key=len).lower() if words else "task"
        W = w[:1].upper() + w[1:]
        if CODEX:
            work = [(f"⏺ Bash(rg -n \"{w}\" src)", f"⎿ src/{w}.rs:42: fn {w}()"),
                    (f"⏺ Read(src/{w}.rs)", "⎿ Read 188 lines"),
                    (f"⏺ Edit(src/{w}.rs)", "⎿ +6 -2"),
                    ("⏺ Bash(cargo test)", "⎿ test result: ok. 64 passed; 0 failed")]
        else:
            work = [(f"⏺ Search(pattern: \"{w}\", path: \"Sources\")", "⎿ Found 4 files"),
                    (f"⏺ Read(Sources/{W}View.swift)", "⎿ Read 212 lines"),
                    (f"⏺ Update(Sources/{W}View.swift)", f"⎿ Updated Sources/{W}View.swift with 6 additions and 2 removals"),
                    ("⏺ Bash(swift test)", "⎿ Executed 212 tests, with 0 failures")]
        yield ("sleep", 0.5)
        for call, result in work:
            self.add_line(call)
            yield ("sleep", 0.4)
            self.add_line(result)
            yield ("sleep", 0.5)
        self.fold_queue()
        said = " ".join((self.turn_prompt or prompt or "the task").split())
        said = said if len(said) <= 70 else said[:69] + "…"
        self.finish(f"Done: {said}. Two files changed and all 212 tests pass.", f"handled \"{said[:40]}\"", 6, 2)

    def run_director(self, value=None):
        self.waiting = None
        while self.gen:
            try:
                req = self.gen.send(value)
            except StopIteration:
                self.gen = None
                return
            value = None
            if req[0] in ("sleep", "wait"):
                self.waiting = (req[0], time.monotonic() + req[1])
                return
            if req[0] == "prompt":
                if self.unclaimed is not None:
                    value, self.unclaimed = self.unclaimed, None
                    continue
                self.waiting = ("prompt", None)
                return
            self.waiting = (req[0], None)
            return

    def later(self, dt, fn):
        self.timers.append((time.monotonic() + dt, fn))

    # ---- input ----
    def submit(self, text):
        cmd = text.strip()
        if cmd in ("/exit", "/quit") and (CODEX or cmd == "/exit"):
            return self.exit("prompt_input_exit", command=True)
        if cmd == "/login":
            self.add(("you", cmd))
            self.add(("out", "Signed in." if CODEX else "Login successful"))
            if self.reported and self.reported[1] == "auth" and not self.turn_open:
                self.report("idle")
            return
        if cmd == "/clear" and not CODEX and not self.turn_open:
            self.report("working")
            self.hook("SessionEnd", reason="clear", prompt_id=self.prompt_id)
            self.report("idle")
            self.sid = str(uuid.uuid4())
            self.entries = [("header", "")]
            self.full = True
            self.hook("SessionStart", source="clear", session_title=self.title_base or "")
            return
        if cmd == "/compact" and not CODEX and not self.turn_open:
            self.report("working")
            self.hook("PreCompact", trigger="manual", custom_instructions="", prompt_id=self.prompt_id)
            self.add(("you", cmd))
            self.add(("out", "Compacted (ctrl+o to see full summary)"))
            self.later(1.5, self.compacted)
            return
        if self.turn_open or self.asking:
            self.queue.append(text)
            self.dirty = True
            # claude submits a queued prompt at once, within the running turn.
            self.hook("UserPromptSubmit", prompt=text, prompt_id=self.prompt_id, permission_mode=self.mode())
            return
        self.start_turn(text)

    def compacted(self):
        self.hook("SessionStart", source="compact", model=self.o["model"] or "standin", prompt_id=self.prompt_id)
        self.hook("PostCompact", trigger="manual", compact_summary="The conversation so far.", prompt_id=self.prompt_id)
        self.report("done", msg=self.last_summary)

    def keylog(self, line):
        folder = os.path.join(HARNESS, "keylog")
        if os.path.isdir(folder) and safe_name(self.sid):
            with open(os.path.join(folder, self.sid + ".log"), "a") as f:
                f.write(line + "\n")

    def insert(self, text):
        self.input = self.input[:self.cur] + text + self.input[self.cur:]
        self.cur += len(text)
        self.dirty = True

    def key(self, k):
        self.keylog(k)
        self.dirty = True
        if self.dialog:
            return self.dialog_key(k)
        if k != "ctrl-c":
            self.ctrl_c_at = None
        if k != "esc":
            self.esc_at_idle = None
        a = self.asking
        if k == "enter":
            if a:
                if self.input.strip():
                    return self.answer(self.input.strip())
                if a["sel"] < len(a["options"]):
                    return self.answer(a["options"][a["sel"]])
                return
            text = self.input
            if text.endswith("\\") and self.cur == len(text):  # a trailing backslash makes Return a newline
                self.input, self.cur = text[:-1] + "\n", len(text)
                return
            if not text.strip():
                return
            self.input, self.cur = "", 0
            return self.submit(text)
        if k == "newline":
            return self.insert("\n")
        if k == "esc":
            if self.turn_open and not a and self.escape_asks:
                # Once: a CLI that asks before it stops.
                q, self.escape_asks = self.escape_asks, None
                return self.ask(q["ask"], q.get("options", []), q.get("header"))
            if self.turn_open or a:
                return self.interrupt()
            if self.input and not CODEX:
                # A second Escape soon after the first clears the line.
                if self.esc_at_idle and time.monotonic() - self.esc_at_idle < 0.8:
                    self.input, self.cur, self.esc_at_idle = "", 0, None
                else:
                    self.esc_at_idle = time.monotonic()
            return
        if k == "ctrl-c":
            if self.turn_open or a:
                return self.interrupt()
            if self.input:
                self.input, self.cur = "", 0
                if not CODEX:
                    # claude clears the line and arms the exit at once.
                    self.ctrl_c_at = time.monotonic()
                    self.later(2.05, lambda: setattr(self, "dirty", True))
                return
            if self.ctrl_c_at and time.monotonic() - self.ctrl_c_at < 2:
                return self.exit("prompt_input_exit")
            self.ctrl_c_at = time.monotonic()
            self.later(2.05, lambda: setattr(self, "dirty", True))
            return
        if k == "ctrl-d":
            if not self.input and not self.turn_open and not a:
                return self.exit("prompt_input_exit")
            return
        if k in ("up", "down") and a:
            a["sel"] = (a["sel"] + (1 if k == "down" else -1)) % (len(a["options"]) + 1)
            return
        if k == "backspace" and self.cur:
            self.input = self.input[:self.cur - 1] + self.input[self.cur:]
            self.cur -= 1
        elif k == "delete":
            self.input = self.input[:self.cur] + self.input[self.cur + 1:]
        elif k == "left":
            self.cur = max(0, self.cur - 1)
        elif k == "right":
            self.cur = min(len(self.input), self.cur + 1)
        elif k == "home":
            self.cur = self.input.rfind("\n", 0, self.cur) + 1
        elif k == "end":
            nl = self.input.find("\n", self.cur)
            self.cur = len(self.input) if nl < 0 else nl
        elif k == "ctrl-u":  # to the start of the line; at the start, joins with the line above
            start = self.input.rfind("\n", 0, self.cur) + 1
            start = start - 1 if start == self.cur and start else start
            self.input = self.input[:start] + self.input[self.cur:]
            self.cur = start
        elif k == "ctrl-w":
            m = re.search(r"\S*\s*$", self.input[:self.cur])
            self.input = self.input[:m.start()] + self.input[self.cur:]
            self.cur = m.start()

    def char(self, ch):
        self.keylog("char " + ch)
        if self.dialog:
            return
        a = self.asking
        if a and not self.input and ch.isdigit() and 1 <= int(ch) <= len(a["options"]):
            return self.answer(a["options"][int(ch) - 1])
        if a:
            a["sel"] = len(a["options"])
        self.ctrl_c_at = None
        self.insert(ch)

    CONTROL = {0x0d: "enter", 0x0a: "newline", 0x7f: "backspace", 0x08: "backspace", 0x03: "ctrl-c",
               0x04: "ctrl-d", 0x15: "ctrl-u", 0x17: "ctrl-w", 0x01: "home", 0x05: "end", 0x02: "left",
               0x06: "right", 0x1b: "esc"}

    def parse(self):
        b = self.inbuf
        i = 0
        now = time.monotonic()
        while i < len(b):
            if self.pasting:
                end = b.find(b"\x1b[201~", i)
                if end < 0:
                    keep = max(i, len(b) - 5)
                    self.paste += b[i:keep]
                    i = keep
                    break
                self.paste += b[i:end]
                i = end + 6
                self.pasting = False
                text = self.paste.decode("utf-8", "replace").replace("\r\n", "\n").replace("\r", "\n")
                self.paste = b""
                self.keylog("paste " + json.dumps(text))
                if self.asking:
                    self.asking["sel"] = len(self.asking["options"])
                self.insert(text)
                continue
            c = b[i]
            if c == 0x1b:
                if i + 1 >= len(b):
                    if self.esc_at is None:
                        self.esc_at = now + 0.05
                        break
                    if now < self.esc_at:
                        break
                    self.esc_at = None
                    self.key("esc")
                    i += 1
                    continue
                self.esc_at = None
                n = b[i + 1]
                if n == 0x5b:  # CSI
                    m = re.compile(rb"\x1b\[([0-9:;<=>?]*)([ -/]*)([@-~])").match(b, i)
                    if not m:
                        if re.fullmatch(rb"\x1b\[[0-9:;<=>?]*[ -/]*", b[i:]):
                            break
                        i += 2
                        continue
                    self.csi(m.group(1).decode(), m.group(3).decode())
                    i = m.end()
                    continue
                if n == 0x5d:  # OSC: a reply from the terminal
                    m = re.compile(rb"\x1b\]([^\x07\x1b]*)(\x07|\x1b\\)").match(b, i)
                    if not m:
                        if re.fullmatch(rb"\x1b\][^\x07\x1b]*\x1b?", b[i:]):
                            break
                        i += 2
                        continue
                    if m.group(1).startswith(b"7501;?") and not self.status_ok:
                        self.status_ready()
                    i = m.end()
                    continue
                if n == 0x4f:  # SS3
                    if i + 2 >= len(b):
                        break
                    k = {0x41: "up", 0x42: "down", 0x43: "right", 0x44: "left", 0x48: "home", 0x46: "end"}.get(b[i + 2])
                    if k:
                        self.key(k)
                    i += 3
                    continue
                if n in (0x0d, 0x0a):  # Option-Return
                    self.key("newline")
                i += 2
                continue
            if c < 0x20 or c == 0x7f:
                k = self.CONTROL.get(c)
                if k:
                    self.key(k)
                i += 1
                continue
            size = 1 if c < 0x80 else 2 if c < 0xe0 else 3 if c < 0xf0 else 4
            if i + size > len(b):
                break
            self.char(b[i:i + size].decode("utf-8", "replace"))
            i += size
        self.inbuf = b[i:]

    def csi(self, params, final):
        if final == "~":
            k = {"200": None, "3": "delete", "1": "home", "4": "end", "7": "home", "8": "end"}
            p = params.split(";")[0]
            if p == "200":
                self.pasting = True
            elif k.get(p):
                self.key(k[p])
            return
        if final in "ABCDHF" and not params.startswith("?"):
            self.key({"A": "up", "B": "down", "C": "right", "D": "left", "H": "home", "F": "end"}[final])
            return
        if final == "u" and params and params[0].isdigit():  # kitty keyboard protocol
            parts = params.split(";")
            code = int(parts[0].split(":")[0])
            mods = (int(parts[1].split(":")[0]) if len(parts) > 1 and parts[1] else 1) - 1
            if code == 13:
                self.key("newline" if mods & 1 else "enter")
            elif code == 27:
                self.key("esc")
            elif code == 127:
                self.key("backspace")
            elif code == 9:
                pass
            elif mods & 4 and 64 <= (code & ~0x20) <= 95:
                k = self.CONTROL.get(code & 0x1f)
                if k:
                    self.key(k)
            elif mods in (0, 1) and code >= 32:
                self.char(chr(code))

    # ---- drawing ----
    def size(self):
        s = os.get_terminal_size(1)
        return max(5, s.lines), max(20, s.columns)

    def render(self, entry, cols):
        kind, text = entry
        if kind == "header":
            return self.header(cols)
        if kind == "plain":
            return text
        if kind == "rule":
            label = f"─ {text} "
            return GREY + label + "─" * max(0, cols - cells(label)) + RESET
        lines = text.split("\n")
        if CODEX:
            if kind == "you":
                return "\r\n".join(pad([(("› " if i == 0 else "  ") + line, BOLD if i == 0 else "")], cols, SHADE)
                                   for i, line in enumerate(lines))
            if kind == "tool":
                m = re.match(r"([A-Za-z]+)\((.*)\)$", text)
                name, args = (m.group(1), m.group(2)) if m else (text, "")
                verb = {"Bash": "Ran", "Read": "Read", "Edit": "Edited", "Update": "Edited", "Write": "Added",
                        "Grep": "Searched", "Search": "Searched", "Glob": "Listed"}.get(name, name)
                return f"{GREY}•{RESET} {BOLD}{verb}{RESET} {args}"
            if kind == "out":
                return GREY + "  └ " + text + RESET
            if kind == "err":
                return RED + "■ " + text + RESET
            return "\r\n".join(("• " if i == 0 else "  ") + line for i, line in enumerate(lines))
        if kind == "you":
            return "\r\n".join(GREY + ("❯ " if i == 0 else "  ") + line + RESET for i, line in enumerate(lines))
        if kind == "tool":
            m = re.match(r"([A-Za-z]+)\((.*)\)$", text)
            if m:
                return f"{GREEN}⏺{RESET} {BOLD}{m.group(1)}{RESET}({m.group(2)})"
            return f"{GREEN}⏺{RESET} {text}"
        if kind == "out":
            return "\r\n".join(GREY + ("  ⎿ " + NBSP if i == 0 else "     ") + line + RESET for i, line in enumerate(lines))
        if kind == "err":
            return RED + "  ⎿ " + NBSP + text + RESET
        return "\r\n".join((WHITE + "⏺" + RESET + " " if i == 0 else "  ") + line for i, line in enumerate(lines))

    def header(self, cols):
        if CODEX:
            rows = [f"  {GREY}>_ {RESET}{BOLD}OpenAI Codex{RESET}{GREY} (v{VERSION}){RESET}", f"     {GREY}{self.folder}{RESET}"]
            if self.o["skip"]:
                rows.append(f"  {GREY}permissions:{RESET} YOLO mode")
            rows += ["", "  To get started, describe a task or try one of these commands:", ""]
            rows += [f"  {BOLD}{c}{RESET}{GREY} - {what}{RESET}" for c, what in (
                ("/init", "create an AGENTS.md file with instructions for Codex"),
                ("/status", "show current session configuration"),
                ("/permissions", "choose what Codex is allowed to do"),
                ("/model", "choose what model and reasoning effort to use"),
                ("/review", "review any changes and find issues"))]
            return "\r\n".join(rows)
        model = self.o["model"] or "Stand-in model"
        effort = f" with {self.o['effort']} effort" if self.o["effort"] else ""
        return "\r\n".join([
            f"{ORANGE} ▐▛███▛█ {RESET}  {BOLD}Claude Code{RESET} {GREY}v{VERSION}{RESET}",
            f"{ORANGE}▝▜██████▀{RESET}  {GREY}{model}{effort} · Stand-in plan{RESET}",
            f"{ORANGE}  ▝▝  ▝▝ {RESET}  {GREY}{self.folder}{RESET}"])

    def editor_rows(self, width, first, rest):
        """The input text as rows of `width` cells with the cursor drawn in."""
        rows, row, used = [], [], 0
        text = self.input + " "
        for i, ch in enumerate(text):
            if ch == "\n":
                if i == self.cur:
                    row.append((" ", INV))
                rows.append(row)
                row, used = [], 0
                continue
            w = cells(ch)
            if used + w > width:
                rows.append(row)
                row, used = [], 0
            if i == self.cur:
                row.append((ch, INV))
            elif i < len(self.input):
                row.append((ch, ""))
            used += w
        rows.append(row)
        return [[(first if n == 0 else rest, "")] + r for n, r in enumerate(rows)]

    def dynamic(self, rows, cols):
        now = time.monotonic()
        d = [[]]
        a = self.asking
        working = self.turn_open and not a
        if self.dialog:
            d += self.dialog_rows()
        elif CODEX:
            if working:
                d.append([("• ", GREY), ("Working", BOLD), (f" ({elapsed(now - self.turn_started)} • esc to interrupt)", GREY)])
            if self.queue:
                d.append([("• ", GREY), ("Messages to be submitted after next tool call", ""),
                          (" (press esc to interrupt and send immediately)", GREY)])
            for q in self.queue:
                d.append([("  ↳ " + " ".join(q.split()), GREY)])
            if a:
                d.append([("• ", ""), (a["q"], BOLD)])
                for n, opt in enumerate(a["options"] + [self.input or "Type something else"]):
                    d.append([("› " if n == a["sel"] else "  ", BLUE), (f"{n + 1}. {opt}", BLUE if n == a["sel"] else "")])
                d.append([])
            if len(d) > 1:
                d.append([])
            room = max(1, rows - len(d) - 4)
            if self.input or not a:
                ed = self.editor_rows(cols - 2, "› ", "  ")[-room:]
                if not self.input and not a:
                    ed = [[("› ", ""), ("A", INV), ("sk Codex to do anything", GREY)]]
                for r in ed:
                    d.append(("shade", r))
            d.append([])
            effort = self.o["effort"] or "medium"
            title = f" · {self.title_base}" if self.title_base else ""
            d.append([(f"  {self.o['model'] or 'stand-in'} {effort} · {self.cwd}{title}", GREY)])
            d.append([("  Ctrl-C again to quit" if self.ctrl_c_at else "  ← for agents · ? for shortcuts", GREY)])
        else:
            for q in self.queue:
                d.append([("❯ " + " ".join(q.split()), GREY)])
                d.append([("  ⎿ " + NBSP + "Queued · ctrl+enter to send now", GREY)])
            if self.queue:
                d.append([])
            if working:
                d.append([(SPIN[int(now * 8) % len(SPIN)] + " " + self.step + "… ", ORANGE),
                          (f"({elapsed(now - self.turn_started)} · ↓ 120 tokens)", GREY)])
                d.append([])
            if a:
                d.append([("─" * cols, BLUE)])
                d.append([(" ☐ " + a["header"], BLUE)])
                d.append([])
                d.append([(a["q"], BOLD)])
                d.append([])
                for n, opt in enumerate(a["options"] + [self.input or "Type something."]):
                    sel = n == a["sel"]
                    cursor = [(" ", INV)] if n == len(a["options"]) and sel and self.input else []
                    d.append([("❯ " if sel else "  ", BLUE), (f"{n + 1}. {opt}", BLUE if sel else "")] + cursor)
                d.append([])
                d.append([("Enter to select · ↑/↓ to navigate · Esc to cancel", GREY)])
            else:
                room = max(1, rows - len(d) - 5)
                ed = self.editor_rows(cols - 2, "❯" + NBSP, "  ")[-room:]
                if not self.input:
                    hint = ("Press up to edit queued messages" if self.queue
                            else 'Try "edit <filepath> to…"' if not self.prompts_seen and not self.resumed else "")
                    ed = [[("❯" + NBSP, ""), (hint[:1] or " ", INV), (hint[1:], GREY)]]
                d.append([("─" * cols, GREY)])
                d += ed
                d.append([("─" * cols, GREY)])
            if self.status_text:
                d.append([("  " + self.status_text, GREY)])
            if self.ctrl_c_at:
                d.append([("  Press Ctrl-C again to exit", GREY)])
            else:
                left = "  ⏵⏵ bypass permissions on (shift+tab to cycle)" if self.o["skip"] else "  ? for shortcuts"
                d.append([(left, PINK if self.o["skip"] else GREY)] + ([(" · esc to interrupt", GREY)] if working else []))
        out = []
        for r in d[-rows:]:
            if isinstance(r, tuple):
                out.append(pad(r[1], cols, SHADE))
            else:
                out.append(fit(r, cols)[0])
        return out

    def draw(self):
        rows, cols = self.size()
        out = ["\x1b[?2026h"]
        if self.full:
            out.append("\x1b[H\x1b[2J\x1b[3J")
            self.printed = max(0, len(self.entries) - 2000)
            self.full = False
        elif self.dyn_rows:
            out.append("\r" + (f"\x1b[{self.dyn_rows - 1}A" if self.dyn_rows > 1 else "") + "\x1b[J")
        for e in self.entries[self.printed:]:
            out.append(self.render(e, cols) + "\r\n")
        self.printed = len(self.entries)
        dyn = self.dynamic(rows, cols)
        out.append("\r\n".join(dyn))
        self.dyn_rows = len(dyn)
        out.append("\x1b[?2026l")
        self.write("".join(out))
        self.dirty = False

    # ---- lifetime ----
    def status_ready(self):
        """The terminal answered the 7501 query: from now on claude reports."""
        self.status_ok = True
        self.refresh_title()
        if self.dialog:
            self.report("blocked", kind="permission", msg="trust this folder")
            return
        # A new session with a first prompt reports `working` first.
        if not (self.first_prompt and not self.resumed):
            self.report("idle")
        self.begin()

    def begin(self):
        """Startup is over: the script starts, then the first-prompt argument is submitted."""
        if self.begun or self.dialog:
            return
        self.begun = True
        self.gen = self.director()
        self.run_director()
        if self.first_prompt:
            self.submit(self.first_prompt)

    def start(self):
        self.saved = termios.tcgetattr(0)
        tty.setraw(0)
        self.write("\x1b[?2004h\x1b[?25l" + ("" if CODEX else "\x1b[>5u"))
        r, w = os.pipe()
        os.set_blocking(w, False)
        self.wake_r = r
        signal.set_wakeup_fd(w)
        signal.signal(signal.SIGWINCH, lambda *_: setattr(self, "winch", True))
        for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIGINT):
            signal.signal(sig, lambda n, _: setattr(self, "signal", n))
        if CODEX:
            self.refresh_title()
            if self.script.get("update"):
                self.dialog = {"kind": "update", "sel": 0}
            else:
                self.codex_started()
        else:
            self.refresh_title()
            if self.script.get("trust"):
                self.dialog = {"kind": "trust", "sel": 0}
            else:
                self.session_started()
            self.write("\x1b]7501;?\x07")
            # Without an answer Claude still works, but reports only in its title.
            self.later(1.0, self.begin)
        self.draw()

    def session_started(self):
        """claude's hooks run only in a trusted folder."""
        self.trusted = True
        self.hook("SessionStart", source=self.source,
                  **({"model": self.o["model"] or "standin"} if self.source == "startup"
                     else {"seconds_since_last_response": 60, "context_tokens": 45000,
                           "prompt_cache_likely_expired": False, "estimated_cache_write_usd": 0.7}))
        self.statusline()

    def codex_started(self):
        """codex reports idle, then works for a moment unless a first prompt starts a turn at once."""
        if self.first_prompt:
            if not self.resumed:
                self.report("idle")
            self.later(0.1, self.begin)
            return
        self.report("idle")
        self.report("working")
        self.later(0.5, lambda: self.report("idle"))
        self.later(0.6, self.begin)

    # ---- start-up dialogs ----
    DIALOGS = {"trust": ["No, exit", "Yes, I trust this folder"],
               "update": ["Update now", "Skip", "Skip until next version"]}

    def dialog_rows(self):
        kind, sel = self.dialog["kind"], self.dialog["sel"]
        options = self.DIALOGS[kind]
        if kind == "trust":
            rows = [[("─" * 60, GREY)], [(" Accessing workspace:", BOLD)], [], [(" " + self.cwd, "")], [],
                    [(" Quick safety check: Is this a project you created or one you trust?", "")], [],
                    [(" Claude Code'll be able to read, edit, and execute files here.", "")], []]
            rows += [[(" ❯ " if n == sel else "   ", BLUE), (o, BLUE if n == sel else "")] for n, o in enumerate(options)]
            return rows + [[], [(" Enter to confirm · Esc to cancel", GREY)]]
        rows = [[(f"  Update available · {VERSION} → 0.172.0", BOLD)], [("  Release notes: https://github.com/openai/codex/releases/latest", GREY)], []]
        rows += [[("› " if n == sel else "  ", BLUE), (f"{n + 1}. {o}", BLUE if n == sel else "")] for n, o in enumerate(options)]
        return rows + [[], [("  enter continue · esc skip", GREY)]]

    def dialog_key(self, k):
        d = self.dialog
        n = len(self.DIALOGS[d["kind"]])
        if k in ("up", "down"):
            d["sel"] = (d["sel"] + (1 if k == "down" else -1)) % n
            return
        if d["kind"] == "trust":
            if k == "enter" and d["sel"] == 1:
                self.dialog = None
                self.full = True
                self.report("clear")
                self.session_started()
                self.report("idle")
                return self.begin()
            if k in ("enter", "esc", "ctrl-c"):
                self.report("clear")
                return self.exit("other", code=1)
            return
        if k == "enter" and d["sel"] == 0:
            self.write("\r\n(stand-in) the update would run now\r\n")
            return self.exit("other")
        if k in ("enter", "esc"):
            self.dialog = None
            self.full = True
            self.codex_started()

    def loop(self):
        while True:
            now = time.monotonic()
            due = [t for t, _ in self.timers]
            if self.waiting and self.waiting[1] is not None:
                due.append(self.waiting[1])
            if self.esc_at:
                due.append(self.esc_at)
            if self.turn_open and not self.asking:
                due.append(now + 0.25)
            timeout = max(0.0, min(due) - now) if due else None
            ready, _, _ = select.select([0, self.wake_r], [], [], timeout)
            if self.wake_r in ready:
                os.read(self.wake_r, 512)
            if 0 in ready:
                try:
                    data = os.read(0, 65536)
                except OSError as e:
                    if e.errno != errno.EIO:
                        raise
                    data = b""  # the terminal closed
                if not data:
                    self.signal = signal.SIGHUP
                self.inbuf += data
            if self.signal:
                n = self.signal
                return self.exit("other", code=128 + n, hung=n == signal.SIGHUP)
            if self.winch:
                self.winch = False
                self.full = True
                self.dirty = True
            if self.inbuf:
                self.parse()
            now = time.monotonic()
            for item in [t for t in self.timers if t[0] <= now]:
                self.timers.remove(item)
                item[1]()
            if self.waiting and self.waiting[1] is not None and self.waiting[1] <= time.monotonic():
                self.run_director()
            if self.turn_open:
                self.dirty = True
                if CODEX:
                    self.refresh_title()
            if self.dirty:
                self.draw()

    def exit(self, reason, code=0, command=False, hung=False):
        self.hung = hung
        if CODEX:
            self.title("")
            self.report("clear")
        else:
            if command:
                self.report("working")
            for _ in range(2 if command else 3):
                self.report("clear")
            self.title("")
        if self.dyn_rows:
            self.write("\r" + (f"\x1b[{self.dyn_rows - 1}A" if self.dyn_rows > 1 else "") + "\x1b[J")
            self.dyn_rows = 0
        if CODEX:
            self.write(f"\r\nTo continue this session, run:\r\n  {BOLD}codex resume {self.sid}{RESET}\r\n"
                       + (f"Or run codex resume and select {self.title_base}.\r\n" if self.title_base else ""))
        self.write("\x1b[?25h\x1b[?2004l" + ("" if CODEX else "\x1b[<u"))
        if hung:
            try:
                termios.tcsetattr(0, termios.TCSADRAIN, self.saved)
            except termios.error:
                pass  # the terminal is gone; nothing to restore
        else:
            termios.tcsetattr(0, termios.TCSADRAIN, self.saved)
        self.hook("SessionEnd", reason=reason, prompt_id=self.prompt_id)
        sys.exit(code)


def running_sessions():
    """The stand-in claude sessions running now, in the shape of the real
    `claude agents --json`: one entry per process given --resume ID or
    --session-id ID."""
    found = []
    out = subprocess.run(["/bin/ps", "-axo", "pid=,args="], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout
    for line in out.splitlines():
        pid, _, args = line.strip().partition(" ")
        words = args.split()
        at = next((i for i, w in enumerate(words) if w.endswith("/bin/claude")), None)
        if at is None or int(pid) == os.getpid():
            continue
        rest = words[at + 1:]
        for flag in ("--session-id", "--resume"):
            if flag in rest and rest.index(flag) + 1 < len(rest) and not rest[rest.index(flag) + 1].startswith("-"):
                found.append({"pid": int(pid), "sessionId": rest[rest.index(flag) + 1], "kind": "interactive",
                              "status": "idle", "cwd": "", "name": "", "startedAt": 0})
                break
    return found


def main():
    argv = sys.argv[1:]
    if any(a in ("--version", "-v", "-V") for a in argv):
        print(f"codex-cli {VERSION}" if CODEX else f"{VERSION} (Claude Code)")
        return
    if any(a in ("--help", "-h") for a in argv):
        print(__doc__)
        return
    o = parse_args(argv)
    if not CODEX and o["words"][:1] == ["agents"]:
        print(json.dumps(running_sessions()))
        return
    if not CODEX and o["words"][:2] == ["auth", "status"]:
        print(json.dumps({"loggedIn": True, "authMethod": "claude.ai", "apiProvider": "firstParty"}))
        return
    if CODEX and o["words"][:2] == ["login", "status"]:
        print("Logged in using ChatGPT")
        return
    if not os.isatty(0):
        sys.exit(f"{PROG}: the stand-in needs a terminal")
    app = StandIn(o)
    app.start()
    app.loop()


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
